      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Common Issues"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As with any new technology, users may encounter some common challenges when working with the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Gemma"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " models. One frequent misconception is assuming that smaller models like "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Gemma 3n"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " can perform equally well as larger models in all tasks. While Gemma 3n is highly capable, understanding its limitations is crucial for optimal use. Another issue is related to the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Graphics processing unit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " requirements; ensure your hardware meets the necessary specifications for smooth operation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A common problem is running out of GPU memory when using larger "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Gemma"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " models. To mitigate this, try reducing the batch size or using mixed precision techniques. Another challenge is ensuring that you have the latest versions of required libraries like "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "transformers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "timm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Keep your dependencies updated to avoid compatibility issues."
        }
      ]
    },
